PROVENANCE AND VALIDATION (r2).
- Rows: rows_r2.json, 45 rows, built by build_rows_r2.py from in_E1.json and the filed SVG. The builder asserts:
  - the SVG's, note v0.5's and the patched preprint's sha256;
  - one row per matcher unit, in order;
  - each unit on its node;
  - every quote it adds on its source line (N3 @09c3a8c:385, read by git show; note v0.5 :3 and :78; N8 @09c3a8c:161; preprint :141; F1a node 41);
  - the TS rows' field: three keys, the unit inside the note_quote, its {field, previous: null} record;
  - that only S11#18's and S11#19's successors are discrepant;
  - no scratch path in any row string.
- Official harness (v05_harness.py --rows E1/rows_r2.json --out E1/report_r2.json): 45 rows, 23 figures, 0 unexplained failures, 0 explained, 0 exemptions, 0 corrections, 0 coverage misses on touched lines.
  - Coverage for the file: matcher_units 45, rows 45, none without a row, none beyond.
  - History-schema problems 0. Quotation-scan hits 0: a first r2 build quoted N8's 15-word section heading in full; it was shortened.
  - discrepant_without_nr_disc 2: the TS rows, expected, because the harness's NR_DISC is empty.
  - All four routed files hash to their routed values. Dev status counts for F1a: reproduced 19, computed-new 2, discrepant 2. The harness ran scripts/audit_note_N1.py (sha256 52bfd8d4…f9a3, unmodified since fd2b136).
- The round-9 check (probe/probe_r6_r2.py) ran on a frozen copy of the round-9 machinery (sha256 fca07c77…b428). On the r2 TS rows as given, it fails only the note-line lookup. With nodes 17-19 joined, it passes, and nr_validate_row reports no failure. See FOR THE ROUND-9 PROFILE (5).
- Mutation checks on r2 (copies under mut_r2/):
  - status flipped: 23 of 23 figure rows fail;
  - locator line moved to :1: 23 of 23 fail;
  - source_value digits shifted: 22 of 23 fail. The survivor is again the word unit 'four' (node 7), the validator's leniency, as in r1 and v0.4's S11#11.
- Pins: item raws @09c3a8c, N8 @02b6a61 (the B2b rows) and @09c3a8c (the e2d heading), the N4 correction raw @e60b633, the record @bbc9ffe, README-NOTE.md @fd2b136. HEAD at the r2 run: e3bef6f (r1 ran at 9bf36ad; the commit between them is G-CAL's LOCK-m-F0 and touches no pinned path). The tag note-2026-10-v1 does not yet exist.
- No repo file was written, and there were no git writes; git ran read-only (show, status, rev-parse, log, diff --quiet). git status --short was identical before and after every r2 run. Its modified-file set is the one at the session's start (paper_analysis.ipynb, the N4-N8, N12 and N17 audit scripts); none of those files is E1's.
- Python ran with -B. E1's scratch directory holds build_rows_r2.py, rows_r2.json, report_r2.json, harness_r2.log, span_notes_r2.py, span_notes_r2.json, probe/ (the machinery snapshot, its rows input, probe_r6_r2.py and its output, the status snapshots), mut_r2/, n3c_09c3a8c.json (git show of the N3c JSON), and the r1 files, which are kept.
